	abstract = {The reduction and removal of surface oxides from GaAs substrates by atomic layer deposition(ALD) of Al 2 O 3 and Hf O 2 are studied using in situ monochromatic x-ray photoelectron spectroscopy. Using the combination of in situdeposition and analysis techniques, the interfacial “self-cleaning” is shown to be oxidation state dependent as well as metal organic precursor dependent. Thermodynamics, charge balance, and oxygen coordination drive the removal of certain species of surface oxides while allowing others to remain. These factors suggest proper selection of surface treatments and ALD precursors can result in selective interfacial bonding arrangements.},
