	keywords = {nanoparticles, Nanoparticles, Transmission electron microscopy, Gold, Si, Nanowires, Chemical vapour deposition, Au, Ge, Si substrate, Germanium, WHISKERS, and epitaxy (A6855), Semiconductor growth, structure, Thin film growth, Elemental semiconductors, Nanometre-scale semiconductor fabrication technology (B2550N), quantum wells and related structures (B2530C), Semiconductor superlattices, Low-dimensional structures: growth, structure and nonelectronic properties (A6865), Structure of solid clusters, and nanostructured materials (A6146), Crystal orientation, TRANSPORT, GERMANIUM NANOWIRES, Catalysis, Chemical vapour deposition (A8115H), Chemical vapour deposition (B0520F), Decomposition, Elemental semiconductors (B2520C), Heterogeneous catalysis at surfaces and other surface reactions (A8265J), Nanowire growth, SURFACE, Crystal defects, Crystal morphology and orientation (A6150J), Ge Si, Ge-Si, High resolution transmission electron microscopy, Au catalysis, Au containing nanoparticles, Au0.6, Au0.6Ge0.4, Ausub 0.6, Ausub 0.6Gesub 0.4, Chemically vapor deposited Ge nanowire, Conventional electronic device integration, Crystal lattice, Crystalline defects, Defects in crystals (A6170), Epitaxially oriented nanowires, Ge0.4, Gesub 0.4, Low temperature growth, Nanowire structure, Semiconductor epitaxial layers, Single crystal, Substrate crystal structure, Vapor liquid solid process, VLS process},
