	abstract = {The stability of long, narrow Si nanowires grown by catalytic decomposition of a Si-containing gas during annealing was investigated because their use in devices will depend on their stability during subsequent processing. The nanowires can be annealed without visible change well above 900degreesC in N-2 after air exposure. However, annealing in a H-2 ambient more readily degrades their structure. Nanowires without a native surface oxide are stable up to 850degreesC, but change significantly at 900degreesC. Surface diffusion appears to be sufficient to allow constant-diameter nanowire regions to form.},
