	keywords = {Silicon, Fatigue, Air, Si, and cracks (A6220M), brittleness, fracture, Crystalline Solids [933.1], Elemental semiconductors, Semiconducting silicon, Single crystals, Single Element Semiconducting Materials [712.1.1], Mechanical Properties [421], Strength of Building Materials, Machining Operations [604.2], Elemental semiconductors (B2520C), N, Chemical Products Generally [804], Fracture toughness, Micromachining, ROOM-TEMPERATURE, CERAMICS, Crack propagation, LIFE PREDICTION, PROPAGATION, Single crystal silicon, Stress corrosion cracking, Stress analysis, 10sup 4 to 10sup 10 m/s, 150 micron, 24 h, Apparent stress corrosion threshold, Applied stress intensity, Crack growth exponent, Crack growth rate, CYCLIC FATIGUE, Dry nitrogen, ELECTRON-MICROSCOPY, FRACTURE-TOUGHNESS, Humid air, Metals Corrosion [539.1], Micromachined specimens, N2, NATIVE OXIDE, Nitrogen, Nsub 2, Size 1.5E-04 m, Stress corrosion process, Stress intensity, STRESS-CORROSION CRACKING, Subcritical crack growth, Time 8.6E+04 s, TO-DUCTILE TRANSITION, Velocity 1.0E-10 to 1.0E-04 m/s},
