	abstract = {We have measured the fracture toughness, Ksub Ic, of the LFA110RTA crystal plane in micro-machined silicon structures fabricated using a common deep reactive ion plasma etch process. Crack initiation occurred at surface features left by the etch process. Wide scatter in the notch toughness (0.96-1.65 MPa msup 1/2), presumably due to a distribution of surface flaws, was measured in 11 samples. The data fit a Weibull distribution with E 4.84. Crack propagation in the sample occurred as a series of discrete fracture events interspersed with periods of no growth. (11 Refs.)},
